# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
EN = {
    "hunt_cataclysm": {
        "title": "Cataclysm", "subtitle": "Eight dungeons, eight bosses and weapons found nowhere else",
        "intro": [
            "L_Ender's Cataclysm adds no ores and no machines. It adds reasons to leave the house: eight enormous structures, each holding something that will kill you on the first attempt.",
            "There's no progression in the usual sense — there's an order by difficulty. You start in the Nether at the Soul Forge and finish on the Burning Arena, where Ignis waits.",
            "Boss weapons can't be crafted from anything else and have no equivalents. That's the whole point.",
        ],
        "quests": {
            "root": {"title": "First Find", "text": [
                "The mod scatters abandoned spires, temples and villages across the world — you'll stumble on them without looking. Inside are black steel and ancient metal: the gear you wear to the first boss.",
                "The first accessories come from there too: the vitality ankh, the berserker soul amulet, the ring of the grudged. The belt of the beginner takes two leather and an iron ingot and opens a talisman slot.",
                "The Explorer's Compass finds any of the mod's structures by name. Craft an eye instead, though: eight different eyes each lead to their own structure, the way an eye of ender leads to a stronghold."]},
            "soulforge": {"title": "Soul Forge", "text": [
                "The monstrous eye leads into the Nether, to the Soul Forge. The Netherite Monstrosity sleeps there: six hundred health, twenty-five damage a swing and a habit of pounding the ground hard enough to throw you off it.",
                "It wakes on its own the moment you come close. Killing it is the earliest feat available and the door into the rest of the mod, because it drops the Infernal Forge.",
                "The Forge is a pickaxe with four damage and nearly three thousand durability, and a right-click on a block hits everything around it. Both the Void Forge and Brontes grow out of it later."]},
            "citadel": {"title": "Ruined Citadel", "text": [
                "The void eye points at a citadel in the End. Ender Golems and Endermaptera patrol it, and deep inside the Altar of Void raises the Ender Guardian: three hundred and thirty-three health and twenty armor, the highest of any boss in the mod.",
                "The Guardian drops the Gauntlet of Guard — a right-click drags every living thing in sight toward you. The golems drop the Void Core.",
                "The core is not a trophy but a part. You will need it to turn the Infernal Forge into the Void Forge."]},
            "factory": {"title": "Ancient Factory", "text": [
                "The mech eye leads underground, thirty blocks below zero, to a plant that has run without people for a very long time. The Prowler and the Watcher walk the floors, and in the far hall lies the Harbinger's deactivated frame.",
                "It will not wake by itself: the frame has to be touched with a nether star. After that three hundred and ninety health stand up and come for you, and everything on the floor labelled EMP switches on with them.",
                "The Harbinger drops a block of witherite, nine ingots at once. That is the mod's key metal: the mechanical fusion anvil, the wither assault shoulder weapon, the laser gatling and the meat shredder all come from it."]},
            "fusion": {"title": "Fusion", "text": [
                "The mechanical fusion anvil does what no workbench can: it melts two finished trophies into a third that otherwise does not exist.",
                "Infernal Forge and Void Core give the Void Forge, which fires a fan of void runes. Gauntlet of Guard and Bulwark of the Flame give the Gauntlet of Bulwark. Gauntlet of Guard and Sandstorm in a Bottle give the Gauntlet of Maelstrom. The shoulder weapon plus a void core turns void.",
                "The list of fusions is finite, and each one wants trophies from different bosses. That is Cataclysm's real progression tree."]},
            "pyramid": {"title": "Cursed Pyramid", "text": [
                "The desert eye leads to a pyramid where the Necklace of the Desert lies under suspicious sand. The Ancient Remnant sleeps beside it and reacts to nothing at all until someone clicks it with that necklace.",
                "Then come four hundred and fifty health, twenty-five damage and the curses of the desert. Victory pays out a Sandstorm in a Bottle, the Remnant Skull and a block of ancient metal.",
                "The bottle is more than a weapon: on the fusion anvil it turns the Cursed Bow into the Wrath of the Desert and the Gauntlet of Guard into the Gauntlet of Maelstrom."]},
            "sunken": {"title": "Sunken City", "text": [
                "The abyss eye points at a city on the floor of a deep ocean. Deeplings live there, and the Coralssus, and on the Altar of Abyss the Leviathan: four hundred health and complete invulnerability out of water.",
                "You summon it with an abyssal sacrifice: a nautilus shell, an athame from a deepling priest, crystallized coral, and one block each of diamond, emerald, iron, gold and amethyst with a heart of the sea alongside.",
                "Before the fight, visit the Altar of Amethyst in the same city: it turns amethyst crab meat into the blessed kind, and that grants immunity to Darkness, Abyssal Fear and Abyssal Burn. Without it you fight blind.",
                "The Leviathan drops the Tidal Claws — right-click fires a grapple, left-click strikes with a tentacle."]},
            "acropolis": {"title": "Acropolis", "text": [
                "The storm eye leads to a warm ocean and makes you look up: the Acropolis floats in the sky, at height two hundred. Getting there is a problem of its own.",
                "Inside are Clawdian with its claw, the Hippocamtus, the Cindaria and Scylla herself: three hundred and ninety health and eighteen damage.",
                "She sheds Lacrima and Essences of the Storm, and out of those you forge Ceraunus, an anchor you throw, and Astrape, a spear that fires lightning. Astrape and the Infernal Forge on the fusion anvil give Brontes, which can be thrown."]},
            "frosted": {"title": "Frosted Prison", "text": [
                "The cursed eye leads to snowy plains, to a prison ringed by an abandoned spire, temple and village. Draugr and Aptrgangr walk inside, and the latter always drop the Strange Key, which opens the Door of Seal.",
                "Behind the door stands the Cursed Tombstone. It charges for about a minute before it can be clicked, and then it releases Maledictus: four hundred and twenty health, a cursed rider.",
                "His metal, cursium, makes the ghost armor: the helmet sees through walls, the chestplate revives its wearer on five hearts, the leggings give a chance to ignore a hit outright, the boots soften every fall. Cursium also forges the Soul Render and the Cursed Bow."]},
            "burning": {"title": "Burning Arena", "text": [
                "The flame eye leads to the nether wastes, to a round arena over lava. Ignis waits until Burning Ashes are placed on the Altar of Fire; the Ignited Revenants walking nearby carry them.",
                "The fight runs in three phases, at two thirds and one third of his health. His damage scales off your maximum health, so a big health pool will not save you. He breaks the floor, he holds a shield, and only a void rune punches through it.",
                "After his death Ignited Berserkers start appearing in nether fortresses. And his ignitium makes armor that walks on lava and the Incinerator, a claymore that sets everything in front of it alight."]},
            "ignitium": {"title": "Ignitium Armor", "text": [
                "The upgrade template takes four nether bricks, four blaze powder and a vanilla netherite template; after that it's a smithing table and ignitium over netherite.",
                "The helmet lays a Blazing Brand on a keypress, the leggings answer a hit with flame, the boots walk lava like stone. The chestplate merges with an elytra on the fusion anvil — the only way to fly without taking your armor off.",
                "Cursium armor is its opposite: where ignitium takes the hit, cursium lets you avoid it. Keep both full sets in a chest and swap by situation."]},
            "pets": {"title": "Pets", "text": [
                "Three bosses leave more than weapons behind. The netherite effigy releases the Ministrosity, tamed with a lava power cell. The remnant skull calls the Modern Remnant, tamed with a sniffer egg. The abyssal egg gives the Baby Leviathan.",
                "All three fight for you and, unlike wolves, survive meeting a boss."]},
            "all_bosses": {"title": "Every Last One", "text": [
                "Eight bosses: the Netherite Monstrosity, the Ender Guardian, the Harbinger, the Ancient Remnant, the Leviathan, Scylla, Maledictus and Ignis.",
                "The mod keeps score and grants the advancement when the list runs out. It's one of the longest hunts in the pack.",
                "If you want to kill one of them twice, a Boss Respawner is left where five of them fell: click it with the right eye and the owner comes back."],
                "rewards": ["A complete trophy hall"]},
        },
    },
    "hunt_beasts": {
        "title": "Beasts and Mutants", "subtitle": "Alex's Mobs, Mowzie's Mobs and Mutant Monsters",
        "intro": [
            "Three mods fill the world with the life vanilla was missing: from harmless capybaras to bosses you build an arena for.",
            "Alex's Mobs is a hundred creatures with their own habits and useful drops. Mowzie's Mobs is four staged boss fights. Mutant Monsters is vanilla mobs allowed to grow up.",
        ],
        "quests": {
            "dictionary": {"title": "Animal Dictionary", "text": [
                "Alex's Mobs adds well over a hundred creatures, and remembering who lives where and eats what is hopeless. The dictionary answers both questions: a book, green dye and any item from the mod.",
                "Twenty-one animals can be tamed. A grizzly follows honey, a gorilla bananas, a capuchin rides your shoulder, a kangaroo carries your things in its pouch, and a laviathan ferries four passengers across lava."]},
            "tame": {"title": "Taming", "text": [
                "An elephant is tamed with an acacia blossom, a bald eagle with fish oil, a tarantula hawk with a spider eye, a mantis shrimp with tropical fish, a warped toad with mosquito larva.",
                "Some are not tamed but calmed. A tiger fed meat grants the Tiger's Blessing, froststalkers follow whoever wears their helmet, and the undead stop noticing the owner of an unsettling kimono.",
                "The falconry glove lets you carry an eagle on your arm and loose it at a target; the hood lets you steer it directly."]},
            "locators": {"title": "Echolocation", "text": [
                "Cachalot whales sometimes beach themselves. Save one and you get ambergris, and ambergris with two whale teeth and an iron ingot builds the echolocator, which points at the nearest cave.",
                "Four ender pearls turn it into the endolocator, which hunts for stronghold portal frames. No more digging for a stronghold at random."]},
            "beast_gear": {"title": "Gear from the Hunt", "text": [
                "Half the useful things in Alex's Mobs are built from what its own creatures drop. Two tarantula hawk wings and an elytra give an elytra that never breaks. Seven centipede legs give leggings you climb walls in.",
                "Eight crocodile scutes speed up your swimming, eight rocky shells turn a sprint into a roll, three lost tentacles and a crossbow become a grapple.",
                "The vine lasso catches any creature, hostile ones included, and carries it in your pocket."]},
            "voidworm": {"title": "Void Worm", "text": [
                "A crimson mosquito larva goes into a capsid, the container you take off an enderiophage. The larva becomes a mysterious worm.",
                "The worm is thrown into the void of the End. Out of it rises the Void Worm, the mod's largest opponent, which splits apart as you fight it.",
                "It drops an eye and mandibles, and those with two netherite ingots build the dimensional carver: a portal back to your spawn point from anywhere. The shattered version, crafted inside a capsid, reaches a million blocks."]},
            "transmute": {"title": "Transmutation Table", "text": [
                "A nether star, two farseer arms and three obsidian make a table that converts whole stacks of items into one another for experience.",
                "It is not automation and not a factory. It is a way to unload the chests of whatever piled up too high and get what ran short."]},
            "wroughtnaut": {"title": "Ferrous Wroughtnaut", "text": [
                "Mowzie's Mobs hides a wrought chamber underground, and Ferrous Wroughtnaut stands inside it. He does not move until someone comes close, and he will not be hit from the front: a two-hundred-and-twenty-degree arc is sealed.",
                "The one window is the moment after he slams the axe into the ground and the blade sticks. Strike from behind, and only then.",
                "Victory pays an axe and a helmet, both unbreakable. The axe cuts in a wide arc, and crouching turns the swing into a shockwave along the ground."]},
            "frostmaw": {"title": "Frostmaw", "text": [
                "A Frostmaw sleeps in snowy biomes: two hundred and fifty health and an ice crystal in its paw. Wake it head-on and it swallows the crystal; kill it and it gives the crystal back.",
                "There is a second road: creep within two blocks of the paw while invisible and simply take the crystal. Then a music disc drops from the body instead, but only while it rains.",
                "The crystal never breaks and restores itself. Holding right-click raises a blizzard, and after three seconds it applies Frozen, a full lock on all actions for two and a half seconds. Fire ends it early."]},
            "umvuthi": {"title": "Umvuthi", "text": [
                "An Umvuthana grove stands in the savanna. Arrive without a mask and the whole village, Umvuthi the Sunbird included, comes at you. Arrive in a mask taken from a raptor and Umvuthi sells the Sun's Blessing for seven blocks of gold, and gives it free every time after.",
                "The blessing lasts an hour and grants four moves with an empty hand: Sunstrike and Solar Flare for free, Solar Beam for five minutes of the reserve, and Supernova for everything that is left.",
                "Kill Umvuthi anyway and the Sol Visage remains, a helmet that never breaks. Wearing it, any Umvuthana mask turns into an ally on a right-click, and you can keep ten of those at once."]},
            "sculptor": {"title": "The Sculptor's Trial", "text": [
                "A monastery stands on the mountain peaks, and its keeper, Tongbi the Sculptor, is not hostile to you. Bluffs live inside: forty-five health and eighteen damage, the most dangerous rank-and-file mobs in the mod. They drop bluff rods.",
                "Hand a rod to the Sculptor and he sets a trial: climb sixty blocks in four hundred seconds, placing and breaking nothing, no teleports, no flight. Pure parkour.",
                "The reward for finishing is guaranteed: the Earthrend Gauntlet. It lifts boulders out of the ground, tunnels through earth and pushes its owner up on a pillar of soil.",
                "You can kill the Sculptor instead, but then one random item of five drops, and the gauntlet is one chance in five."]},
            "chemx": {"title": "Chemical X", "text": [
                "Mutant Monsters works two ways. Mutants spawn on their own, but at a twentieth of the usual weight, so the meeting is random and always badly timed.",
                "The second way is reliable. A thick potion brewed with an endersoul hand, a hulk hammer, a creeper shard or a mutant skeleton skull becomes Chemical X. Splash it on a zombie, skeleton, creeper, enderman or snow golem and you get the mutant version. A pig becomes a spider pig, but only if you feed it a fermented spider eye first.",
                "A mutant zombie is durable three times over: it stands up again and again until the fallen body is set alight with flint and steel. It drops the hulk hammer, which sends a seismic wave along the ground."]},
            "mutant_gear": {"title": "Mutant Trophies", "text": [
                "A mutant skeleton falls apart on death: skull, ribs, limbs, pelvis, shoulder pads. Those build an armor set that protects about as well as iron, repairs with bone blocks, and carries three hidden traits: the boots grant permanent Jump Boost, the leggings Speed, and the skull on your head makes any bow fire like Multishot.",
                "A mutant enderman leaves an endersoul fragment. Drop an eye of ender beside it and you get the endersoul hand: right-click teleports you where you're looking with no fall damage.",
                "A charged creeper minion egg, when it hatches wrong, yields a creeper shard, which detonates around its owner, throwing back everything alive and poisoning the owner as payment."]},
            "combat": {"title": "The New Combat", "text": [
                "Better Combat throws out the aim ray and counts a hit as the weapon's volume intersecting the target's hitbox. A sword sweeps a hundred and twenty degrees, a dagger or claymore a hundred and fifty, a glaive up to a hundred and eighty.",
                "Reach is now an attribute and is printed in the tooltip: a dagger reaches two and a half blocks, a sword three, a scythe three and a half, a spear four. A sword has three attacks in its combo, a katana four, and the combo resets after three idle seconds.",
                "Two-handed weapons will not tolerate a shield in the off-hand; any one-handed weapon, on the other hand, can be held in both, striking alternately and a fifth faster.",
                "Cataclysm's weapons are mapped by a separate datapack: the Incinerator counts as a claymore, the Soul Render as a halberd, Ceraunus as an anchor, and the forges as hammers."],
                "tasks": ["Read: every weapon has its own arc and its own reach"]},
        },
    },
}
